  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas remain pinched between a leading edge of the monsoon \ntrough and an embedded col to the north-northeast. Southwesterly \nflow buckling against the col, in addition to upper-level divergence,\nis allowing for numerous showers and isolated thunderstorms with \nlocally heavy showers this evening. Most of the activity is occurring\nover the coastal waters, but a few thunderstorms moving over the \nislands cannot be ruled out. The col will gradually continue moving \nto the northwest, inducing a shift from westerly to northerly winds \nin the coming days, as well as showers tapering down to isolated on \nLabor Day. Later in the week, the easterly trade winds will return, \npossibly remaining light to gentle. Shower coverage for next week may\ndiffer as model guidance hints at a potential circulation developing\nto the east of the islands. Due to the high uncertainty regarding \nthis pattern, showers top out at 30 percent through the end of next \nweek. This will continue to be refined as confidence naturally \nincreases with time.",
